<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>An open contact pair must perturb nothing</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-06</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      The ContactPatchTest2d blocks with the upper body raised by 0.1 so the interface starts
      open, and BOTH bodies supported independently -- neither needs the interface. The applied
      1e6 Pa compresses them by O(1e-5), four orders of magnitude too little to close the gap.

      With applyContactForce="yes" the contact forms are therefore assembled with an EMPTY
      active set on every Newton iteration. That is the code path this test exists for: the "no
      active point on this segment" branch of both ContactABInt and ContactLinInt, which has to
      hand the assembler a correctly shaped zero block built from the equation counts rather
      than a matrix of size zero. Every other force-carrying contact test has at least one
      active point on its single segment, so that branch had never executed.

      The result must be identical to the same model with no contactList at all.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactOpen2d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="plane">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="planeStrain">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="block_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- both bodies stand on their own; the interface is not a load path here -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <fix name="top">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- A body force rather than a surface pressure, because every free surface of this
               model is either a Dirichlet boundary or the contact interface itself: a pressure
               on `top` would be swallowed by its own fixed support and leave the solution
               identically zero, which would make the test vacuous. The acceleration is scaled
               up to 1e4 m/s^2 so both bodies deform by O(1e-4): large enough to be a real
               solution, still three orders below the 0.1 gap, so the interface stays open. -->
          <volumeAcceleration name="master_elem">
            <comp dof="x" value="0"/>
            <comp dof="y" value="-1e4"/>
          </volumeAcceleration>
          <volumeAcceleration name="slave_elem">
            <comp dof="x" value="0"/>
            <comp dof="y" value="-1e4"/>
          </volumeAcceleration>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
